{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01KkXer3PuPWtwGkqPiMtvNp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-folder personal productivity + R&D mission-control system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no siblings). Grounded from the project docs:\n\n- **It's a GTD-style task manager backed by plain markdown.** Tasks, projects, inbox, cancelled/saved archives, and per-domain files (academic, commercial, family, writing) are all markdown â€” the source of truth. There's no database. Tasks move through a lifecycle: active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored.\n\n- **It ships a local web app, `anchor_gui.py`** â€” the declared deliverable and primary interface. A self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that regenerates the full dashboard HTML on each request, writes directly to the markdown files, and runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`.\n\n- **It has a CLI mirror, `anchor.py`** â€” same logic as the GUI, generates the static `dashboard.html`, and exposes read-only `rnd` inspection subcommands.\n\n- **Its centerpiece is an R&D \"Project Cockpit\"** for driving the planning/build trio (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). Each project window is a single-screen cockpit where each lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) is a tile with one honest status light, and clicking expands an inline panel pairing a cached summary with a real, resizable terminal â€” no page navigation.\n\n- **The terminal substrate is real ConPTY** (via the one declared native exception, `pywinpty`, lazy-imported in `pty_manager.py` only), with per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry under `.anchor/`, an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini), and proactive cached project/session summaries. Everything else stays Python-stdlib-only.\n\n- **It self-tests daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every markdown file, exercising every endpoint on a throwaway port, and walking the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (never the live service or real `claude`).\n\n- **Current state:** the R&D surface is built through **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (9 waves GREEN, 637 tests passed) and merged to master as of 2026-06-13.\n\nThis was a grounded read of the project's own docs â€” no code execution or external lookups needed for a description-level summary."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c272b65-8dcb-46e4-a788-b118e4534a36","uuid":"af964679-dc46-4986-8a9f-ec3b398f8691","request_id":"req_011Cc1Jeu4ovXKv92CkbXKZa"}
